# rules.pdl (rmmc skin of vox, D137) - copy of @.apps/vox/rules.pdl with the island numbers: the world is 216 x 156 columns (x 0..215, z = desk row 0..155) and 41 levels high (the tallest peak is level 28, vox y 30 with RULE shift 3); hunger is OFF (a rule value, not a code branch).
RULE | world_x_max | 215
RULE | world_y_max | 40
RULE | world_z_max | 155
RULE | reach | 4
RULE | stack_max | 64
RULE | place_needs_support | 1
RULE | move_max | 4
RULE | wait_max_turns | 10000
RULE | turns_move | 1
RULE | turns_mine | 1
RULE | turns_place | 1
RULE | minutes_per_turn | 10
RULE | day_minutes | 1440
RULE | start_minute | 420
RULE | sleep_max_light | 3
RULE | sleep_bed_reach | 3
RULE | sleep_wake_minute | 420
# TOOL | name | power (a swing of the block's tool_best uses that tool's power; any other tool swings at the hand's power)
TOOL | hand | 1
TOOL | shovel | 2
TOOL | axe | 2
TOOL | shears | 2
TOOL | pick | 3
# DAYLIGHT | minute | level 0..15 (linear between rows, integer division toward zero; the sky and rules read this, nothing stores a time of day)
DAYLIGHT | 0 | 2
DAYLIGHT | 300 | 2
DAYLIGHT | 360 | 8
DAYLIGHT | 420 | 15
DAYLIGHT | 1080 | 15
DAYLIGHT | 1140 | 8
DAYLIGHT | 1200 | 2
DAYLIGHT | 1440 | 2
# hunger on manual turns (D110): every spawned actor gains hunger_per_turn on each TURN row (cap hunger_max); at starve_at mine and place refuse (22); EAT lowers hunger by food_<item> and costs turns_eat
RULE | hunger_per_turn | 0
RULE | hunger_max | 40
RULE | starve_at | 30
RULE | turns_eat | 1
RULE | food_apple | 4
RULE | food_bread | 12
# walking (D137; read by vox_op walk and jump): a walk is ONE MOVE row of manhattan length 1 + |dy|, so move_max must be at least 1 + the larger of step_up and fall_max (1 + 3 = 4)
RULE | step_up | 1
# climbing out of water: the shore of a lake is 2 above its shallow bed, so a wader may step up 2
RULE | fall_max | 3
RULE | water_max_depth | 1
RULE | jump_height | 1
RULE | step_up_wade | 2
# crafting (2026-11-25): a station block must be within craft_reach; each craft is one turn
RULE | craft_reach | 2
RULE | turns_craft | 1
# RECIPE | name | out item | out n | in1 | n1 | in2 | n2 | station (- = none)      the out item of a recipe is what the hotbar slot picks: pick the item you want, press C
RECIPE | planks | planks | 4 | wood_side | 1 | - | 0 | -
RECIPE | table | craft_table | 1 | planks | 4 | - | 0 | -
RECIPE | pickaxe | pick | 1 | planks | 3 | - | 0 | craft_table
RECIPE | axe | axe | 1 | planks | 3 | - | 0 | craft_table
RECIPE | shovel | shovel | 1 | planks | 2 | - | 0 | craft_table
# guns (D158, owner 2026-11-27: "give one of their tools to be guns .22, auto/bazooka"): a held item that has a GUN row is FIRED by the use key (b) instead of swung. The ammo is a bag item taken by the SHOT row.
# GUN | name | ammo item | effect (dmg ignite water) | dmg per round | range (cells) | rounds per pull (ammo used) | blast radius | dmg lost per cell of distance | max hardness it can chip | turns per shot | deposit kind (- none)
GUN | pistol22 | bullets   | dmg    | 1 | 24 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 2 | 1 | -
GUN | autogun  | bullets   | dmg    | 1 | 20 | 5 | 0 | 0 | 4 | 1 | -
GUN | bazooka  | rockets   | dmg    | 8 | 30 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 6 | 2 | -
GUN | flamer   | fuel      | ignite | 0 | 6  | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | -
GUN | watergun | waterpack | water  | 0 | 10 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | water_f3
RULE | indestructible_hardness | 99
RULE | eye_height | 1
RULE | muzzle_height | 0
RULE | pitch_run | 2
# fire and water (D159): a BURN row says what a flammable block (the blocks.pdl flammable column) does on fire: BURN | kind | turns it burns | percent chance per turn that a burning neighbour sets it alight | what it becomes
RULE | fire_seed | 7
RULE | fire_cells_per_turn | 32
RULE | extinguish_char_pct | 50
RULE | flow_cells_per_turn | 16
RULE | water_spread | 3
RULE | water_dry_turns | 8
BURN | wood_side | 6 | 25 | charcoal
BURN | wood_top | 6 | 25 | charcoal
BURN | planks | 5 | 40 | charcoal
BURN | craft_table | 5 | 30 | charcoal
BURN | leaves | 3 | 60 | air
# ammo and weapons are crafted (the picked hotbar item is what is made, press m; the weapons need a craft_table within reach)
RECIPE | pistol | pistol22 | 1 | planks | 2 | stone | 3 | craft_table
RECIPE | auto | autogun | 1 | planks | 3 | stone | 6 | craft_table
RECIPE | bazookarec | bazooka | 1 | planks | 4 | stone | 8 | craft_table
RECIPE | flamerrec | flamer | 1 | planks | 3 | gravel | 4 | craft_table
RECIPE | watergunrec | watergun | 1 | planks | 3 | sand | 4 | craft_table
RECIPE | bulletsrec | bullets | 12 | gravel | 1 | - | 0 | craft_table
RECIPE | rocketsrec | rockets | 2 | sand | 2 | gravel | 2 | craft_table
RECIPE | fuelrec | fuel | 6 | leaves | 4 | - | 0 | -
RECIPE | waterrec | waterpack | 8 | snow | 2 | - | 0 | -
# vehicles, first cut (D161, owner 2026-11-28 "then we will try car/plane we planned"): a car is ROWS. Derived numbers (mass, top speed, acceleration) are computed from them on every read (vox_op derive / vstate), never stored.
# Units: mass in grams (density kg per cubic metre x volume in cubic decimetres = grams), force in newtons, power in watts, speed in micrometres per second (integer fixed point, no float), time in milliseconds, 1 cell = veh_cell_um micrometres.
# MATERIAL | id | density (kg per m3)
MATERIAL | steel | 7800
MATERIAL | iron | 7200
MATERIAL | alloy | 2700
MATERIAL | rubber | 1100
MATERIAL | fabric | 600
# MODEL | id | length (cells, front-to-back) | width (cells) | height (cells)       the footprint; local cell (f, r): f = 0 at the rear .. length-1 at the nose, r = 0 at the left .. width-1 at the right; the origin is the rear-left cell
MODEL | car | 4 | 2 | 2
# PART | model | id | kind | material | volume (dm3) | attached to (axle id for a wheel, - none)       kinds: chassis axle wheel engine seat door (mass = density x volume, summed)
PART | car | chassis | chassis | steel  | 60 | -
PART | car | axle_f  | axle    | alloy  | 30 | -
PART | car | axle_r  | axle    | alloy  | 30 | -
PART | car | wheel_fl | wheel  | rubber | 30 | axle_f
PART | car | wheel_fr | wheel  | rubber | 30 | axle_f
PART | car | wheel_rl | wheel  | rubber | 30 | axle_r
PART | car | wheel_rr | wheel  | rubber | 30 | axle_r
PART | car | engine  | engine  | iron   | 25 | -
PART | car | seat_l  | seat    | fabric | 60 | -
PART | car | seat_r  | seat    | fabric | 60 | -
PART | car | door_l  | door    | alloy  | 25 | -
PART | car | door_r  | door    | alloy  | 25 | -
# AXLE | model | axle part id | steered (1/0) | driven (1/0)      only DRIVEN axles propel: their wheels carry the drive force
AXLE | car | axle_f | 1 | 0
AXLE | car | axle_r | 0 | 1
# ENGINE | model | engine part id | power (W) | max drive force (N)       drive force = min(max force, power / speed), then capped by the traction of the driven wheels (RULE veh_mu_pct)
ENGINE | car | engine | 14000 | 3500
# SEAT | model | seat id (the word the player uses) | part id | f | r | door id | role (driver can drive)
SEAT | car | driver    | seat_l | 1 | 0 | door_l | driver
SEAT | car | passenger | seat_r | 1 | 1 | door_r | passenger
# DOOR | model | door part id | side (l = left, r = right: the cell beside the car at the seat's f) | key item (a locked door needs it in the bag to be unlocked; - none)
DOOR | car | door_l | l | car_key
DOOR | car | door_r | r | car_key
# VBODY | model | name | f0 | r0 | y0 | f1 | r1 | y1 (sixteenths of a cell from the rear-left-bottom corner, heading local) | r | g | b : the boxes the engine draws (the generic box: event cube), no code per model
VBODY | car | floor  | 0  | 0  | 2  | 64 | 32 | 9  | 60 60 66
VBODY | car | hood   | 40 | 1  | 9  | 64 | 31 | 17 | 200 40 40
VBODY | car | trunk  | 0  | 1  | 9  | 14 | 31 | 17 | 200 40 40
VBODY | car | seat_l | 16 | 4  | 9  | 22 | 14 | 19 | 40 40 50
VBODY | car | seat_r | 16 | 18 | 9  | 22 | 28 | 19 | 40 40 50
VBODY | car | screen | 36 | 1  | 17 | 38 | 31 | 27 | 150 200 230
VBODY | car | wheel_fl | 44 | -2 | 0 | 58 | 4  | 11 | 20 20 20
VBODY | car | wheel_fr | 44 | 28 | 0 | 58 | 34 | 11 | 20 20 20
VBODY | car | wheel_rl | 6  | -2 | 0 | 20 | 4  | 11 | 20 20 20
VBODY | car | wheel_rr | 6  | 28 | 0 | 20 | 34 | 11 | 20 20 20
# vehicle rules (all numbers): dt per drive row, cell size, the most cells one row may move, gravity, rolling resistance (per mille of weight), air drag (milli newtons per (m/s)^2), tyre grip (percent of the driven weight), full brake force,
# reverse drive (percent of forward, speed cap), steering (slowest speed that can turn, speed kept after a turn in percent, drive rows before the next turn), enter reach, the fastest speed one may get out at, ground following, deepest water a car may enter (0 = none)
RULE | veh_dt_ms | 100
RULE | veh_cell_um | 1000000
RULE | veh_max_cells | 8
RULE | veh_g_mms2 | 9810
RULE | veh_roll_permille | 15
RULE | veh_drag_milli | 1200
RULE | veh_mu_pct | 80
RULE | veh_brake_n | 6000
RULE | veh_rev_pct | 40
RULE | veh_rev_max_um | 5000000
RULE | veh_steer_min_um | 1500000
RULE | veh_turn_keep_pct | 85
RULE | veh_steer_cooldown | 3
RULE | veh_enter_reach | 2
RULE | veh_exit_max_um | 2000000
RULE | veh_step_up | 1
RULE | veh_fall_max | 1
RULE | veh_water_max_depth | 0
RULE | veh_notice | 4
RULE | turns_drive | 0
